  "body": "At the moment, it seems that `ctx.getImageData(sx, sy, sw, sh)` returns a newly-allocated `ImageBitmap`, which can be wasteful.\r\n\r\nProposal:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nctx.getImageData(sx, sy, sw, sh, imageBitmap);\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhere the newly added optional `imageBitmap` parameter allows the method to write to an existing ImageData's buffer. If the size does not match, and error is thrown.\r\n\r\nOr maybe there would be an options object, in case of wanting to add more parameters later (but I can't think of any right now):\r\n\r\n```js\r\nctx.getImageData(sx, sy, sw, sh, {imageBitmap});\r\n```",
